{"id":199917810074547,"type":"album","name":"Winter Songs","artist":"Art Bears","year":1979,"weight":15,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711004.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-696ccfcc-a83d-34eb-8422-afd82dff454b/mbid-696ccfcc-a83d-34eb-8422-afd82dff454b-25209281591.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":17,"country":"JP","scaruffi":7.5,"yt":"k1Hu3Gem1dM","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/6fjGCNFTsQb1ICKWfUNNCN","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_lQotFlcjFSnFD8Y-Vp9qUby5iLeXYqBtM","bandcamp":"https://rermegacorp202.bandcamp.com/album/winter-songs","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/art-bears/winter-songs"},"desc":"Winter Songs is the second album by English avant-rock group Art Bears. It was recorded at Sunrise Studio in Kirchberg, Switzerland between 22 November and 5 December 1978, and was released in 1979. It was Art Bears' first album to be recorded on their own, the bulk of their first album, Hopes and Fears (1978) having been recorded as Henry Cow. Winter Songs comprises fourteen short songs composed by Fred Frith around texts by Chris Cutler that were based on carvings on the dado of the west façade of Amiens Cathedral in France. The whole album was recorded and mixed ."},"artist_ref":{"id":10455561261833,"name":"Art Bears","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/03d9a67119ab857b73e56d617e8d37bb/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":265524373450282,"type":"genre","name":"jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1461,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":173341470623130,"type":"genre","name":"avant-garde","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":298,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":259017761383338,"type":"genre","name":"Rock in Opposition","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":83,"yt":null,"src":"rym"}],"lists":[{"id":259136201394021,"name":"RYM Top — Scenes & Movements —